cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "medexplain: an interactive notebook that helps patients understand their medical reports and visit transcripts"
abstract: >-
  A Jupyter notebook and Python package that explains a patient's own radiology,
  pathology and lab reports and doctor-patient conversation transcripts in plain
  language. It runs offline by default: document-type detection with shown evidence,
  section reordering (conclusion first), a curated plain-language glossary with
  NegEx-style negation and uncertainty detection, lab results compared only with the
  reference range printed in the report, extraction of visit instructions and warning
  signs, and generated questions for the care team. An optional, consent-gated
  explanation uses the Claude API on redacted text.
type: software
